course: dictionary
lesson: 281
title: American: a word with a place in it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «American» is an adjective and a noun. It tells you where something comes from or is about. American food is food from America, and an American city is a city in America.
explain: Usually, in school, American means from the United States of America. A person from the United States is also called an American. Read the words around it to check which place is meant.
explain: Sometimes the place is bigger. «Native American peoples» means the first peoples of the Americas as a whole, which means North, Central and South America. Context clues help you see which meaning fits.
explain: Also notice American English. «American spelling dropped the u from words like "color"» shows that American spelling is one kind of English. British English keeps «colour», and both are correct in their own country.
fact: «American» means from or about the United States of America, or from or about the Americas as a whole.
fact: An American is a person from the United States.
fact: American English uses some different words: sidewalk is American for pavement, and fall is American for autumn.
fact: Noah Webster's dictionary of 1828 helped American spelling drop the u, so people write «color» and «favorite» in America.
fact: «The internet began in 1969 by linking a few computers in American universities and grew into a worldwide network.»
exercise: «The internet began in 1969 by linking a few computers in American universities.» Which country are these universities in? | Britain | Scotland | *The United States | Australia
exercise: «Most American tarantulas flick itchy barbed hairs at enemies.» Where do these tarantulas come from? | In the middle of the sea | *In the Americas, North, Central and South America | In Scotland | In Africa only
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means from or about the United States. | spelling | dropped | *American | favorite
exercise: What is the American word for pavement? | fall | trainers | *sidewalk | color
test: What does «an American» mean? | A person who lives on the moon | A kind of spelling | A person from Scotland | *A person from the United States
test: «Native American peoples» means peoples from which place? | Only the city of Washington | The sea | *The Americas as a whole | Only Britain
exam: In «an American football game», what does American tell you? | A type of food | From the Americas as a whole, but never the USA | Something very old | *From or about the United States, like the sport played there
